10
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:32.433
So I actually need to fix that,
and actually start our game.

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.600
Now, in our GameManager Script,
since this is the Script

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.533
that's managing all the different states
that our game is going through.

13
00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:43.733
Like restarting, and game over,

14
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:47.333
we'll add a "StartGame()"
method into this,

15
00:00:47.566 --> 00:00:50.866
so we don't have to keep immediately
starting the game on start.

16
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.133
So, we'll add a new method,
we'll make it public,

17
00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.066
so we can use it outside of this class.

18
00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:01.000
It'll be void, and it'll
be called StartGame().

19
00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:05.200
Luckily, we've already written
code to start our game.

20
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.300
So, we're just gonna use that.

21
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.100
In our Start() method here,

22
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.933
you can see that we have
our different settings.

23
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:15.866
So we'll take all of these,

24
00:01:15.866 --> 00:01:19.100
and we'll cut them out
of our Start() method,

25
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:23.333
and we'll paste all of that code
into our StartGame().

26
00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:25.866
So now when the game is started,

27
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.333
we know that the game is set to active.

28
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:31.233
Our score is reset, and then we can
start spawning all of our enemies.

29
00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:35.866
Make sure we save, and then,
in our difficulty Button Script,

30
00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:39.066
we're actually going to need a reference
to the GameManager,

31
00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:41.100
just like we did in our Target Script.

32
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.933
So this will be private,

33
00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:46.566
and we just need to get our GameManager,
and we'll call it the gameManager,

34
00:01:46.566 --> 00:01:50.400
because that's what it is.
Now, in our Start() method,

35
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.000
we also need to get a reference
to that gameManager.

36
00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:56.733
So we'll get our gameManager variable,

37
00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:02.666
and we'll set it or assign
it to the gameManager = GameObject.

38
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.400
So, if we use GameObject
in our Hierarchy,

39
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.500
we will Find("") the Object
that's called "Game Manager."

40
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.700
And then once we've found that Object,
we'll need to get its Component,

41
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.966
which is handily also
called the GameManager.

42
00:02:27.066 --> 00:02:30.900
And then in our SetDifficulty() method,
we can now use our gameManager.

43
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.900
And we can use the StartGame() method,
that we wrote before.

44
00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:40.633
So, if we test our game now,

45
00:02:40.766 --> 00:02:43.000
nothing should happen,
when we press Play.

46
00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.700
None of those crates are spawning,

47
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.600
but then, if we press one
of our buttons, let's go for easy mode,

48
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.366
there you go you've got
some crate spawning.

49
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.300
And then our game should go over,
get the Game Over, cool.

50
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.100
So we're almost there,
but at least now we can start the game

51
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.066
when we press one of the buttons.

52
00:03:06.066 --> 00:03:09.533
So, what you're gonna do,
in your GameManager Script,

53
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.900
you're going to create a new
method called StartGame().

54
00:03:14.066 --> 00:03:16.800
And then we can just grab
all of the code

55
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.200
from our Start() method at the top,

56
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.666
and paste it down into StartGame().

57
00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:26.000
In our DifficultyButton Script,

58
00:03:26.866 --> 00:03:28.966
create a variable for the GameManager.

59
00:03:29.566 --> 00:03:32.633
Make sure to Find("")
that gameManager in the scene,

60
00:03:33.066 --> 00:03:35.866
and then get the Component
of its GameManager Script,

61
00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.100
so we can get the variables.

62
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.400
And then, in SetDifficulty(),

63
00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.333
you can then call 
gameManager.StartGame();

64
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.900
so, when we click one of the buttons,

65
00:03:46.366 --> 00:03:50.600
it'll then run this line of code,
and start our game. Now it's your turn.

